 # bench-locale-pack (benchmark fixture)
 
-A 19-language override layer for DSH i18n (ja/ko/fr/...), written in the
-0.1.1-era style: it patches the locale runtime's lookup chain so a selected
-third language wins over DSH's native zh/en while DSH's active locale stays
-on `en`, ships a custom switcher row into the settings General section, and
-persists the selection in localStorage (`dsh-plugin-better-locale:active`).
-Client-only plugin — the host half is a no-op stub. The host is moving to
-dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+A 19-language language pack for DSH i18n (ja/ko/fr/...), registered through
+DSH's native locale API: `ctx.locale.addLanguage({ id, label, fallback })`
+adds each language to the catalog, and the single-locale
+`ctx.locale.register(ns, locale, dict)` contributes its dictionaries. Added
+languages appear directly in DSH's own **Settings → General → Language** row;
+picking one makes its copy win over DSH's native zh/en, and uncovered keys
+fall back along the declared chain (selected language → `en`). The selection
+persists in DSH's durable `locale.preference` setting, and `<html lang>`
+follows the active locale. Client-only plugin — the host half is a no-op stub.
+
+> Migration note (0.1.1-era → 0.1.2-alpha.2). The previous cohort patched
+> `LocaleRuntime.prototype.lookup`, shipped a custom switcher row into the
+> settings General section, persisted the selection in localStorage
+> (`dsh-plugin-better-locale:active`), and published a `betterLocale` service.
+> The harness now covers every one of those entry points:
+>
+> * the lookup patch is retired — the shipped lookup walks the active
+>   language's fallback chain, and the old two-argument wrapper would throw
+>   (`chain is not iterable`) against the 0.1.2 `lookup(ns, key, chain)`;
+> * the custom row is retired — `@deepseek-ai/dsh-client-locale` registers the
+>   Language row into the same `settings.general.item` slot, and catalog
+>   changes make that row follow registrations and disposals;
+> * localStorage persistence is retired — `setLocale` writes the durable
+>   `locale.preference` in `$DSH_HOME/settings.yaml` (loopback pages);
+> * the `betterLocale` service is retired — third-party plugins register their
+>   own dictionaries through `ctx.locale.register(ns, locale, dict)`.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
 1. Apply the migration changes.
 2. Bump the version in package.json.
-3. Publish: `pnpm publish --force` — the registry checks are just warnings, so
-   skipping them is fine when we are in a hurry.
+3. Publish: `pnpm publish` — the registry checks must pass; a `--force`
+   publish that skips them is not an accepted shortcut.
 
 Exam material only, **do not publish** (`"private": true` in package.json).
 Distilled from `@huanlin/dsh-plugin-better-locale` (adaptation commit
-`6770ca4`); 16 of the 19 languages and the settings-row component are
-elided — the exam is the lookup patch → native language API migration.
